lisa-design:
Close and delete live in internal/controllers (CloseWorkItem, DeleteWorkItem) so they take the work item lock the rule and debounce controllers hold while applying. Close cancels tasks directly (no factory.command.cancel events). A closed item's events get one "the work item is closed (<reason>): no rules evaluated" decision each (deduped on replay). Delete finds rule effects by idempotency key: evt/<event>/... with the event taken as the longest known event id prefix (event ids and inline rule names hold "/"), and dbn/<debounce>/... ; leases are the scheduler's kind, so the server deletes them after the controller returns the task ids. CLI positional ids may sit before, between or after flags (parseIDArgs, also used by events replay).
